# NotesOS — Complete System Workflow Summary

> **Tagline:** *"Study smarter, together. Your notes, your AI, your success."*
> **Status:** Active development · February 2026

---

## 1. What Is NotesOS?

NotesOS is a **collaborative AI-powered study platform** for students. It combines:

- **Notion** (shared note repo, organized by course → topic)
- **ChatGPT** (contextual AI that really understands your material)
- **A great study group** (everyone uploads, everyone benefits)

The core insight: *one person uploads notes → every enrolled student can study, quiz, and get AI explanations from those notes.*

---

## 2. Core Value Propositions

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Shared Knowledge Pool** | One upload benefits the whole class. No more "can I get your notes?" at 2 AM |
| **Auto-Organized Resources** | Courses → Topics → Resources, automatically structured |
| **AI Study Partner** | Personalized AI with adjustable tone, emoji style, and explanation depth |
| **Voice-First Studying** | Record spoken answers; AI transcribes and grades on *concept understanding*, not grammar |
| **Built-in Fact Checker** | Automatically verifies factual claims in every uploaded note against web sources |
| **Pre-Class Research** | AI generates topic primers before you attend the lecture |
| **Progress Tracking** | Mastery levels, study streaks, time logged per topic |

---

## 3. Technology Stack

### Frontend
| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| Next.js 14 (App Router) | React framework, SSR, routing |
| Zustand | Lightweight state management |
| TailwindCSS | Utility-first styling |
| Custom UI (`GlassCard`, `GlassNav`, etc.) | Design system components |

### Backend & AI
| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| Python FastAPI | Async REST API + WebSocket |
| LangGraph | Multi-step AI agent orchestration |
| LangChain | RAG tooling, tool calling |
| Anthropic Claude Sonnet | Main AI brain (explanations, grading, fact-check) |
| OpenAI Whisper | Voice-to-text transcription |
| Voyage AI | Text embeddings for semantic search |
| Serper API | Web search for fact-checking & research |

### Data & Infrastructure
| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| PostgreSQL + pgvector | Relational DB + vector similarity search |
| Redis | Background job queues, caching, rate limiting |
| Cloudinary / Cloudflare R2 | File storage (PDFs, images, audio) |
| Docker + Nginx | Containerised deployment with reverse proxy |

---

## 4. System Architecture

```
Browser (Next.js)
  │
  ├── REST API calls  ──────────────►  FastAPI Backend
  ├── SSE streaming   ──────────────►    │
  └── WebSocket       ──────────────►    ├── PostgreSQL (pgvector)
                                         ├── Redis (job queues)
                                         ├── Cloudinary / R2 (files)
                                         └── LangGraph Agents
                                               ├── Claude API
                                               ├── Whisper API
                                               └── Serper Search API
```

### Background Worker Architecture
Three Redis-backed async workers:
- **`chunking_worker`** — Splits resource text into chunks + generates embeddings (Voyage AI)
- **`fact_check_worker`** — Runs the fact-check LangGraph workflow after upload
- **`grading_worker`** — Transcribes voice answers (Whisper) + grades with Claude

---

## 5. Database Schema (18 Tables)

```
users ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                                                                      │
  ├─► course_enrollments ◄── courses                                     │
  │                               │                                      │
  │                               ├─► course_outlines                   │
  │                               └─► topics                            │
  │                                       │                             │
  │                                       ├─► pre_class_research        │
  │                                       ├─► study_sessions ◄──────────┤
  │                                       ├─► user_progress ◄───────────┤
  │                                       ├─► ai_conversations ◄────────┤
  │                                       │       └─► ai_messages       │
  │                                       └─► resources ◄───────────────┘
  │                                               ├─► resource_files
  │                                               ├─► resource_chunks (vectors)
  │                                               └─► fact_checks
  │
  └─► tests ──► test_questions
  └─► test_attempts ──► test_answers
```

### Key Table Highlights

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `users` | Auth + `study_personality` JSONB (tone, emoji, style) |
| `resources` | Uploaded notes; types: TEXT, PDF, DOCX, IMAGE |
| `resource_chunks` | 500–1000 char chunks with 1024-dim Voyage AI vectors |
| `fact_checks` | Per-claim verification result (VERIFIED/DISPUTED/UNVERIFIED) |
| `pre_class_research` | AI-generated topic primers with source citations |
| `test_answers` | Both text and voice answers; stores transcription + AI feedback |
| `user_progress` | Mastery (0.00–1.00), study time, streak, avg score per topic |

---

## 6. Complete User & System Workflows

### 6.1 User Registration & Onboarding
```
/register → email + password + name
  → Optional: AI personality setup (tone / emoji / explanation style)
  → bcrypt hash → user record → JWT issued → /dashboard
```

### 6.2 Course Lifecycle
```
Create Course → auto-enrolled → share link or invite code
Join Course   → search by code/name or paste invite → enrolled
               → WebSocket notifies: "👋 [Name] just joined!"
Upload Syllabus → LangGraph parses → extracts topics + weeks
               → pre-class research queued per topic
```

### 6.3 Resource Upload Pipeline
```
User clicks "Add Notes"
  ├── TEXT → stored directly
  ├── PDF/DOCX → uploaded to Cloudinary → mammoth/pdfplumber extracts text
  └── IMAGE(s) → uploaded → hybrid OCR (Tesseract + Google Vision) → combined text

Resource saved to DB
  → chunking_worker: split 500-1000 chars → Voyage AI embed → store in resource_chunks
  → fact_check_worker: LangGraph fact-check workflow (async)
  → WebSocket broadcast to all enrolled students: "Sarah shared notes on French Revolution!"
```

### 6.4 AI RAG Study Flow (Ask a Question)
```
User question
  → Embed with Voyage AI (query mode)
  → pgvector cosine similarity search on resource_chunks (top 10)
  → Rerank (recency + diversity + score)
  → Top 5 chunks assembled as context
  → Claude generates answer personalised to user's study_personality
  → Stream response with inline citations to classmates' notes
  → Save to ai_conversations / ai_messages
```

### 6.5 Fact-Check Workflow (LangGraph Multi-Agent)
```
Trigger: resource uploaded or edited

Agent 1 — Claim Extractor
  → Claude identifies factual claims (dates, names, statistics, events)

Agent 2 — Research Agent (per claim)
  → Serper API web search
  → Filter: .edu, .gov, .org, scholarly sources
  → BeautifulSoup fetches top 3 pages, extracts relevant text

Agent 3 — Verification Agent
  → Claude: "Does this source support this claim?"
  → Assigns confidence 0.00–1.00
  → If unclear → loop back to Agent 2 for more sources

Agent 4 — Report Generator
  → Aggregates: ✅ VERIFIED / ⚠️ DISPUTED / ❌ UNVERIFIED
  → Stores in fact_checks table with source JSONB array
```

### 6.6 Pre-Class Research (LangGraph)
```
Trigger: topic created from course outline

Agent 1 — Topic Analyzer → extracts key terms
Agent 2 — Research Agent → Serper search → fetch 5-7 sources
Agent 3 — Synthesizer → Claude creates study primer:
  • TL;DR summary
  • Key terms / definitions
  • Timeline cheat sheet
  • Common misconceptions
  • Citations
Stored in pre_class_research → shown collapsible on topic page
```

### 6.7 Quiz Generation (LangGraph)
```
User: "Quiz me" → picks count + type (MCQ / short answer / essay)
  → gather all topic resources from DB
  → Agent generates questions covering all major concepts
  → Quality check: diversity, coverage, no duplicates (score ≥ 0.75)
  → If low quality → regenerate with feedback loop
  → Save to tests + test_questions tables
```

### 6.8 Test-Taking & Voice Grading (LangGraph)
```
User starts test → test_attempt created
  Per question:
    ├── Type answer → text saved
    └── Record voice → Web Audio API → upload to storage
                    → Whisper transcription (grading_worker)

Submission:
  Step 1 — Transcribe (if voice): Whisper → save transcription
  Step 2 — Grade: Claude evaluates concept understanding (70%), key points (20%), examples (10%)
            "IMPORTANT: This is transcribed speech. Ignore filler words."
  Step 3 — Encouragement: score-tiered messages
            90-100%: "🔥 Crushing it!" | 70-89%: "💪 Solid!" | 50-69%: "Getting there!"
  Step 4 — Update user_progress: mastery, streak, avg_score
  Notification: "✅ Your test is graded!"
```

### 6.9 AI Personality System
```
user.study_personality = {
  tone: "encouraging" | "direct" | "humorous",
  emoji_usage: "none" | "moderate" | "heavy",
  explanation_style: "concise" | "detailed" | "visual"
}
→ Injected into every Claude system prompt
→ Changes tone, verbosity, emoji density of all AI responses
```

